# Lorehold Charm, second mode: Mawloc ({X}{R}{G}) is in Bot1's graveyard, where X is 0 (CR 202.3e), so its mana value is 2 and it
# is a legal target, beside Bot1's Misshapen Fiend. Bot2's own Misshapen Fiend, discarded to hand size, is a creature card with mana
# value 2 too but in an opponent's graveyard: it is refused ("from your graveyard"). Mawloc returns to Bot1's battlefield
# (with no counters: it was not cast, so ravenous's X is 0).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Mawloc
Misshapen Fiend
Lorehold Charm
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Misshapen Fiend x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Mawloc; Misshapen Fiend)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lorehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Return target artifact or creature card)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Graveyard.Misshapen Fiend)
Bot1.Target(Mawloc)
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mawloc
Bot1.Graveyard = Lorehold Charm; Faithless Looting; Misshapen Fiend
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 1
